# PX4 parameter overrides for the monospinner, layered on top of the x500
# (PX4_SYS_AUTOSTART=4001) baseline. See CLAUDE.md for why we reuse that airframe instead
# of adding one to PX4-Autopilot/.
#
# Format: one `param set <NAME> <VALUE>` per line (blank lines and lines starting with
# `#` are ignored by scripts/run_sim.sh). No values are set yet -- this is scaffolding.
#
# TODO(physics): EKF2_IMU_POS_X/Y/Z must be set to the IMU's offset from the body origin
# (see hub_offset in models/monospinner/model.sdf and the "Known traps" section of
# CLAUDE.md -- a spinning body with EKF2_IMU_POS unset corrupts the velocity estimate via
# uncompensated centripetal acceleration). Left unset until the IMU sensor pose in
# model.sdf is finalized.
#
# TODO(physics): the land detector and several failsafes assume a non-rotating multirotor
# and must be relaxed for a vehicle that spins continuously by design. Exact parameter
# names (e.g. land-detector rotation thresholds) need to be confirmed against
# PX4-Autopilot/src/modules/land_detector once that source is fetched -- not guessed here.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Put ROS 2 /fmu/out/* timestamps on the SIMULATION clock.
#
# With UXRCE_DDS_SYNCT=1 (PX4's default, module.yaml:97) the uXRCE-DDS client adds the
# measured client/agent offset to every outgoing message timestamp:
#   src/modules/uxrce_dds_client/dds_topics.h.em:126
#     int64_t time_offset_us = session->time_offset / 1000;
# so /fmu/out/* arrives in ROS 2 stamped in the AGENT's OS wall-clock time, while Gazebo
# topics are stamped in simulation time. Measured here: gz ground truth at t=96 s against
# a PX4 estimate at t=1788873294 s, i.e. no usable overlap at all.
#
# Setting this to 0 makes the client publish raw hrt_absolute_time(), which under lockstep
# is gz sim time (GZBridge::clockCallback -> px4_clock_settime, GZBridge.cpp:331-347;
# drv_hrt.cpp:106-115). Ground truth and estimate then share one timeline and can be
# overlaid and differenced directly.
#
# This matters more here than on a conventional airframe. Per CLAUDE.md the commanded
# phase is beta_cmd = psi_desired - theta_spin - delta(omega), so a heading estimate that
# LAGS rotates the control input directly. Estimator lag is a control quantity for this
# vehicle, and it cannot be measured at all if the two series are not on one clock.
#
# Note: reboot_required, so it must be set at boot. scripts/run_sim.sh applies this file
# through the PX4_PARAM_* env hook (rcS:129-134) precisely for that reason.
#
# Cost: ROS 2 consumers can no longer relate /fmu/out/* stamps to wall time. For this
# workspace that is the right trade -- everything downstream is sim analysis.
param set UXRCE_DDS_SYNCT 0

# Magnetic declination: deliberately NOT overridden. EKF2_DECL_TYPE stays at its default (3,
# use PX4's WMM). The sim's field is made to match the WMM by the yawed magnetometer <pose>
# in models/monospinner/model.sdf -- see the comment there. Do not set EKF2_DECL_TYPE 0 to
# use a manual EKF2_MAG_DECL: in v1.17 getMagDeclination() (src/modules/ekf2/EKF/
# aid_sources/magnetometer/mag_control.cpp:602-623) then returns 0, not EKF2_MAG_DECL,
# and with bit 1 set EKF2 overwrites EKF2_MAG_DECL with the WMM value anyway
# (EKF2.cpp:2751-2760).
